LINEAGE
The plugin is built against the kennel plugin SDK of Hundekraft 3.0.3 (https://github.com/Hundekraft/op1-workshop),
which is based on op1r-src by pcppcp (https://github.com/pcppcp/op1r-src); both are GPL-3.0-or-later with the same
additional permission (see their LICENSE and NOTICE files). The marker-jump logic ports op1r's tape/markers.c
jump semantics. No Teenage Engineering firmware, device key or NAND image is included or required to build.

REQUIRED CORE
Hundekraft 3.0.3 (kennel feature API OP1_FEATURE_API = 1). Built with the 3.0.3 source/SDK bundle
(SHA-256 of the bundle: 2f745e3858f9fabf8e653ecfe3511679b47f795ff09f13e9bd5590e26995b1d7).
Newer cores may work; older cores reject unknown imports at load time.

WHAT IT DOES (control map)
- Shift + Help (clock mode) -> T3 settings: the "MIDI MAP" switch row (green, white or red depending on
  registration order; it is the only switch registered today). Turn: mapping ON/OFF (setting op1midi.mmen).
- White encoder push in clock mode: opens the mapping editor (modal overlay, 320x160).
- Editor: blue = MIDI channel (1..16 / ALL), green = CC/PC number (push toggles CC <-> PC), white = action
  (turn; push = value edit for TAPE/INSTRUMENT, push again = validate), red = row cursor over 16 rows
  (4 pages, the cursor row is drawn red, others white), left/right = pages, Shift + Help = validate and close
  (settings op1midi.mmr0..mmr15, one packed int32 per row).
- Actions: MARKER NEXT / MARKER PREV (jump via the core's shared markers tm_pos[]/tm_n and
  op1_tape_pos_set), PLAY FROM MARKER (locate + op1_seq_press_play; only from stop, no punch, no armed
  count-in), TAPE SELECT (value 1..4 -> op1_tape_switch), INSTRUMENT SELECT (no core service yet: a toast
  explains it once per boot).
- Mapped CCs are taken from the core's key/encoder path (op1_midi_take_cc). Default mapping (empty user
  config): CC 80 next, CC 81 previous, CC 82 play-from-marker, channel 1.

CLAIMS
- key:clock:white (the white encoder push in clock mode; no other plugin consumes it in 3.0.3).

BUILD
- hundekraft-plugin/build-knl.sh <path to the 3.0.3 source bundle> — packs synth_sdk/plugins/op1midi
  with the bundle's tools/kennel/pack.py inside the bfin-elf Docker toolchain. Output: op1midi.knl.

INSTALL
- Workshop (https://hundekraft.github.io/op1-workshop/): Your plugins -> add op1midi.knl -> Update OP-1 ->
  confirm with T1 on the OP-1 prompt. Takes effect at the confirmed restart. Removal and conflicts are
  managed by the workshop. Save a disk-mode backup first (see install-recuperation.md in the repository).

CHANGES
- v6.8 (2026-10-28): hardware-confirmed v6.7 (pictograms GONE — the firmware glyph/icon atlas
  theory was right; midi learn and key learn work). Three changes:
  (1) KEY LEARN NO LONGER EXITS: with any learn armed (midi or key), no key quits the editor
  (they are swallowed). Escape routes stay: Help validates+closes, white click alone exits
  key learn, Shift+green toggles midi learn. Before this, an accidental mode/transport key
  during the learn window closed the whole editor.
  (2) BLUE CLICK = CLEAR SLOT (Shift+blue click empties the row, same as Shift+red) and
  plain blue click cycles the NOTE DISPLAY MODE, global, persisted as 'mmnd': raw number
  (60) -> english (C#4) -> french solfege (DO#4) -> number. The source cell of NOTE rows
  shows the name accordingly; a toast shows the mode with the cursor row's note as sample.
  (3) LOWERCASE WHERE POSSIBLE: the kennel stroke font has capitals only, so units are drawn
  as SMALL CAPS (half height, baseline-aligned): the shift-held channel shows "ch n" and the
  fade cell shows "1s/2s/8s/32s"; fade toasts are now true lowercase ("fade 1s" — the toast
  font is the firmware's). Stale v7 header (knob roles) corrected.
- v6.7 (2026-10-28): SHIFT CONFIRMED on hardware (v6.6 fix works). Three changes:
  (1) Learn feedback toasts (user request): "midi learn" / "key learn" / "learn off" on
  arming/disarm, "cc N" / "note N" / "pc N" when a MIDI message is captured, "touche N" when
  a sound key is captured, and "key: snd requis" when Shift+white is pressed on a row whose
  destination is not SND (key learn requires SND — this silent refusal is why key learn
  seemed dead: mm2_edit_learn_feed defaults empty rows to TAPE). The per-key "k..." and
  "shift s..." diagnostics are removed.
  (2) PICTOGRAMS: the residual icons at the top-left (mixer/fx/drum/ADSR-like) are the
  firmware's shared glyph+icon atlas flashing through while the R246 Text objects rasterize
  new glyphs — our editor kept re-set strings on 34 native text objects. The editor now
  draws ALL text with the kennel's stroke font (sf_text, uppercase) — zero firmware Text
  objects (bss 6592 -> 336 bytes). If any pictogram survives this, the theory is wrong and
  we look at the veil/panel next.
- v6.6 (2026-10-28): SHIFT FIX. The on-device key log proved the Shift key itself (code 0x26)
  reaches the plugin — but our editor is modal and swallowed the Shift press too. The stock
  dispatch (KEY_DISPATCH) runs AFTER the features' input filter and is what latches the stock
  shift byte (0x01DD7F78); by swallowing 0x26 we kept the byte at 0, so every Shift combo
  arrived with shift=0 (v6.2..v6.5). Fix: pass the Shift press/release through to the stock
  while the editor is open (0x26 is not an exit key; Shift alone does nothing in the stock).
  Temporary confirmation toasts: "shift s1/s0" on Shift press/release and "k<hex><s>" on
  each key press while the editor is open (removed in v6.7). The truncated bottom diag line
  of v6.5 is removed.
- v6.5 (2026-10-28): the v6.4 row fix works on hardware (confirmed) but Shift still does
  nothing. Static analysis says shifted keys DO reach feature input() (the hooked site is
  the common KeyHandler::process_queue dispatch, and the delivered in->shift IS the stock
  byte 0x01DD7F78 — the same one midiseq uses). So we debug on-device: the editor now shows
  a diagnostics line (bottom of the panel): S = live byte at 0x01DD7F78, E = the shift field
  of the last delivered event, A = live byte at 0x019D7C6C (the kn_save.c candidate), and
  k = the last 6 input events as hex code + press/release (encoders with bit 0x80, "v" =
  down turn). Hold Shift and report what it shows. The v6.4 boot toast is removed (its job
  is done). Removed in v6.6 once the shift source is identified.
- v6.4 (2026-10-28): the v6.3 row fix was a NO-OP (the op1_switch call was left in the
  BOOT_DONE branch and sw_pending was never set to 1), so v6.3 behaved exactly like v6.2
  for the settings row — sorry. Now: BOOT_DONE only arms sw_pending, the row is registered
  at the FIRST main-loop SERVICE pass, strictly after midiseq's BOOT_DONE registration →
  MIDI SEQ keeps the first (green) row, MIDI MAP takes the second (white) row. A one-time
  boot toast "midi map v6.4" proves which build actually runs on the device (removed at
  v6.5 once confirmed). Stale mm2_*.c duplicates removed from hundekraft-plugin/op1midi/
  (the build always used mm2/).
- v6.3 (2026-10-28): hardware fixes from the first on-device test. The "MIDI MAP" settings row
  is registered on the FIRST main-loop service pass after boot (after midiseq's BOOT_DONE
  registration) so MIDI SEQ keeps the green row and MIDI MAP takes the white one — the
  BOOT_DONE registration raced with midiseq's. The tape-state guard now accepts BOTH 0 and 3
  as "stopped" (the real R246 stop state; only 0 was accepted before, which left everything
  but MUTE dead on hardware). The Shift state is now read from the STOCK shift byte
  (0x01DD7F78 — the same address the kennel's own markers plugin uses) instead of relying on
  the delivered event field.
- v6.2 (2026-10-28): NATIVE R246 font for the editor overlay (firmware Text objects, built once
